+## Subtopics
+
+### Ellipsoid Partitioning
+Uses an ellipsoid instead of a unit sphere for the foreground volume to achieve tighter bounds on the region of interest [S1].
+
+### Altitude-Constrained Raycasting
+Uses camera altitude measurements to constrain ray sampling bounds, terminating rays near ground level to avoid querying underground regions [S1].
+
+### Geometric Clustering
+A method to partition training images (pixels) into different NeRF submodules based on visibility, enabling data parallelism [S1].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Training Speed:** Improves training speed by 3x compared to baseline approaches on existing datasets [S1].
-*   **Rendering Speed:** Achieves a 40x speedup over conventional NeRF rendering [S1, S3].
-*   **Quality:** Remains within 0.8 dB in PSNR quality compared to conventional NeRF [S1, S3]. Improves PSNR by 12% compared to baseline approaches [S1].
-*   **Scalability:** Scales to scenes 1000x larger than prior work, from 150,000 to over 1,300,000 m² per scene [S1].
-*   **Strengths:** Enables interactive fly-throughs for large-scale urban scenes; efficient training via data parallelism; efficient rendering via spatial locality and temporal coherence [S1].
-*   **Limitations:** Requires visibility analysis for pixel partitioning; relies on camera altitude measurements for optimal culling [S1].
+*   **Time Complexity:** Training is accelerated by 3x compared to baseline approaches [S1]. Rendering achieves a 40x speedup over conventional NeRF rendering [S1][S3].
